      "writtenOn": "2025-06-12T00:13:52Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Why not disable pkvm_enabled_key already?",
      "revId": "c237b9d9b7b0378ffd13f83dad3a85aa1c1ecee6",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "7b23f80d_153fd811",
        "filename": "arch/x86/kvm/vmx/pkvm/pkvm_host.c",
        "patchSetId": 7
      },
      "lineNbr": 1414,
      "author": {
        "id": 3702829
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-06-17T10:50:03Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If we disable pkvm_enabled_key without reprivileging, kernel will be confused about hypercalls as hypercalls are gated behind this static key. Without iommu, there are not much hypercalls, but we have IRQ_REMAP which still uses hypercalls now. So its safe to keep it enabled until we succeed in reprivileging",
      "parentUuid": "33f907b0_7055e9f8",
      "revId": "c237b9d9b7b0378ffd13f83dad3a85aa1c1ecee6",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "d641e202_cca1be68",
        "filename": "arch/x86/kvm/vmx/pkvm/pkvm_host.c",
        "patchSetId": 7
      },
      "lineNbr": 1414,
      "author": {
        "id": 2022314
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-06-17T12:48:58Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I was really hoping we can switch to using pkvm_enabled() instead of enable_pkvm in various places in KVM code, and remove the hack in vmx_init() which resets enable_pkvm to false if vmx_pkvm_init() fails...\n\nCould you elaborate about IRQ_REMAP? Is it expected that kernel is trying to use it even though IOMMU initialization failed?",
      "parentUuid": "7b23f80d_153fd811",
      "revId": "c237b9d9b7b0378ffd13f83dad3a85aa1c1ecee6",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c76d2846_5f9771ed",
        "filename": "arch/x86/kvm/vmx/pkvm/pkvm_host.c",
        "patchSetId": 7
      },
      "lineNbr": 1414,
      "author": {
        "id": 3702829
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-06-17T13:12:42Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "irq remapping is an independent functional block in DMAR, but uses the QI mechanism and is shared with IOMMU. irq remap initialization happens much earlier during apic initialization and it initialized QI as well. Even if IOMMU is disabled, QI will still be active and irq remap logic will access QI through dmar_read/write or our specific hypercalls. So this will hit a snag if we disable the static key without reprivileging. So we need that static key to be enabled for now and I am working on fixing it.",
      "parentUuid": "d641e202_cca1be68",
      "revId": "c237b9d9b7b0378ffd13f83dad3a85aa1c1ecee6",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "8fc0857e_06f3fe1f",
        "filename": "arch/x86/kvm/vmx/pkvm/pkvm_host.c",
        "patchSetId": 7
      },
      "lineNbr": 1414,
      "author": {
        "id": 2022314
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-06-17T15:00:25Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Indeed, you are right, I see intel_prepare_irq_remapping(), intel_enable_irq_remapping() etc are called from apic_intr_mode_init(), which happens much earlier than intel_iommu_init().\n\nDoes this possibly mean that it was a mistake to remove the per-cpu pkvm_enabled variables? Is it possible for any of the functions in drivers/iommu/intel/irq_remapping.c to run on some CPUs in parallel with pKVM deprivileging on other CPUs?\n\n\u003e ...and I am working on fixing it.\n\nCool, thanks.",
      "parentUuid": "c76d2846_5f9771ed",
      "revId": "c237b9d9b7b0378ffd13f83dad3a85aa1c1ecee6",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
