        "id": 3702829
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-06-17T10:50:03Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Fixed the error handling.\n\nI think that its best to have iommu logic outside of vmx_pkvm_init(as the name suggest). Already vmx_pkvm_init is a huge function with lots of error handling and related gotos. Adding to the mix, the case of having to call iommu_init regardless of failures etc will become really complicated. I agree, its doable but not worth it and not as readable as my current implementation. I think this code is much better in terms of readability and logical grouping. I would like to have the code as it is now, please :-)",
      "parentUuid": "1b73a93d_4a78ac60",
